From 24a6522d5e8d1f4cb2fec6c97a86a252560ba425 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:34:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/28] CPU monitor: in words, small in the top left corner;
 warnings when the quality is lowered or voices are cut; Alerts mode

- No white bar any more: small white text on black just behind the letters, in the top left
  corner: "CPU 43%  24 voices" (the CPU average and the voices sounding). The SD times and the
  direness number are gone from the OLED (still in the SysEx for tools/cpu_monitor.html).
- Under it, only when it happens: "quality lowered" while the direness is above 0 (the Deluge
  renders more cheaply to keep up), "voices cut!" while voices are culled because the CPU is
  behind, blinking, and up for 2 s after the last cut. The 7-segment display pops up "CUT".
- Settings > CPU monitor: Off, On, Alerts (only the warnings). Off after every power-up.
- cpu_stats.cpp uses the firmware's snprintf (lib/printf.h), not newlib's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
